<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03QX">Definition <span data-tag="03QX">4.9.2.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a set. We let $|S|$ denote the smallest ordinal $\alpha $ for which there exists a well-ordering of $S$ having order type $\alpha $. We will refer to $|S|$ as the <em>cardinality</em> of the set $S$. A <em>cardinal</em> is an ordinal $\kappa $ which has the form $|S|$, for some set $S$. </p>
